    {
      "id": "oq_t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4534.0,
      "y": 7435.0,
      "width": 1222,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "f5",
      "index": "bAD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 552453320,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 489283772,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793750000000,
      "created": 1793750000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A. Rubber-stamping. If Priya approves 98% of the agent's drafts unchanged, she will start approving without reading.\n  How do we keep her check real: plant an occasional deliberate error to see if she catches it, or track how long she\n  looks at each draft? And who is accountable when a wrong entry she approved reaches Ledgerline?\nB. Conflicting bank evidence. The bank's email says \"credited\" but the statement shows nothing for two days, or the\n  other way round. How long does the agent wait, which source wins, and what does it tell Priya and Emma meanwhile?\nC. Which day's rate? Treasury's rate moves from day to day. Does the comparison use the rate on the day the offer\n  arrives, or on the day of the payment run? And if the rate moves after Vikram decides, is the decision reopened?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "oq",
      "originalText": "A. Rubber-stamping. If Priya approves 98% of the agent's drafts unchanged, she will start approving without reading.\n  How do we keep her check real: plant an occasional deliberate error to see if she catches it, or track how long she\n  looks at each draft? And who is accountable when a wrong entry she approved reaches Ledgerline?\nB. Conflicting bank evidence. The bank's email says \"credited\" but the statement shows nothing for two days, or the\n  other way round. How long does the agent wait, which source wins, and what does it tell Priya and Emma meanwhile?\nC. Which day's rate? Treasury's rate moves from day to day. Does the comparison use the rate on the day the offer\n  arrives, or on the day of the payment run? And if the rate moves after Vikram decides, is the decision reopened?",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
